--- a/textwrap/README.md
+++ b/textwrap/README.md
@@ -4,6 +4,26 @@ Small helpers for laying out plain text in a terminal.
 
 ```js
 import { countWords } from "./src/count.mjs";
+import { wrapText } from "./src/wrap.mjs";
 
 countWords("one two  three"); // 3
+
+wrapText("the quick brown fox jumps", 10); // "the quick\nbrown fox\njumps"
 ```
+
+## `wrapText(text, width)`
+
+Wraps `text` so that no line is longer than `width` characters, and returns the
+wrapped text as a string with its lines separated by `\n`.
+
+- A word is a run of characters that are not whitespace, as in `countWords`.
+  Words are never split, except when a word is longer than `width`: it is then
+  broken into pieces of `width` characters.
+- Each line of `text` (`\n` or `\r\n`) is wrapped on its own, so existing line
+  breaks and blank lines are kept.
+- Within a line, a run of whitespace becomes one space, and whitespace at the
+  start or end of a line is dropped.
+- Width counts code points (a surrogate pair is never split), not display
+  columns.
+- `text` that is not a string, or a `width` that is not a positive integer,
+  throws a `TypeError`.
